{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1032892-horrors-with-many-atavisms","id":1032892,"title":"Horrors with many Atavisms","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-16T13:47:44-08:00","id":1032892,"title":"Horrors with many Atavisms","content":"As a rule, we are told Atavisms, makeup of the Horror, and to a lesser degree Lair Traits tend to reflect each other, the latter two being highly flexible in this regard thank to the malleable dream logic they are built upon. As a character creation thought experiment, let's assume an elder or Incarnate Beast ends up acquiring most or even almost all Atavisms with enough time and effort. Which kind of mythological monster archetype seems most appropriate in the first place for this kind of chimerical Horror ? Assuming the Beast starts with a more 'vanilla' kind of monster concept, how the Horror would end up looking like, after acquiring so many Atavisms ? How the structure and Traits of the Lair would be influenced ? I am driven to think draconic creatures or certain kinds of mythological hybrids (chimeras, griffins, manticores) might be appropriate to represent almost all Atavisms with a few tweaks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 01-17-2017, 04:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T12:37:48-08:00","id":1033557,"title":"","content":"Greek Titan, The Kraken, Dragons, the Devil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T12:42:05-08:00","id":1033562,"title":"","content":"The Gigantes","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T16:32:33-08:00","id":1033718,"title":"","content":"Plus it also depends on how you display it. I know there's a species of turtle real world that feeds on poisonous mushrooms and consequently the turtle itself is toxic to eat. So some atavisms could just be represented as side effects of it's enviorment and eating habits. (Yes I'm picturing an f*ed up version of the whole sword that has killed so many people it catches fire thing being adapted to explain how this thing can breath fire.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T09:26:20-08:00","id":1034063,"title":"","content":"Dragons are an option for sure. Every family has at least one Atavism that fits typical draconic imagery. Chimeras and manticores also make a lot of sense, and I would additionally suggest Echidna and Typhon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T09:42:40-08:00","id":1034083,"title":"","content":"Anything big, smart, with wings would cover the standard Anakim and Ugallu atavisms. Add magic or elementalism or just a big brain and you have Makara.<br /> <br /> Cthulhu, for instance, seems like a Beast version of him would have most Atavisms, lacking only a few like Dragonfire, Shadowed Soul and From the Shadows.<br /> <br /> It's worth keeping in mind the Atavisms are fairly flexible as well. Storm-Lashed is bent towards making a rainstorm, but it could easily be changed to a blizzard, or a sandstorm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-18-2017, 12:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T15:58:27-08:00","id":1034303,"title":"","content":"Horrors based on sorcerers and witches could justify the purchase of many Atavisms as pseudo-spells. Nightmares would work really well as various types of curses and hexes. There could even be a Nightmare gained through Kinship with True Fae and certain Mages that makes the target act in an animalistic manner (and with Satiety Expenditure, actually gives them animalistic body parts).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 01-18-2017, 10:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T03:30:32-08:00","id":1049777,"title":"","content":"Think about something like Ungoliant: Huge, smart, stealthy, deadly, long-limbed, poisonous... Except for Dragonfire, you can probably cram every atavism on her + some of the homebrew stuff from <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas\">here</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T18:01:28-08:00","id":1050190,"title":"","content":"Thinking on it a horror based off a sufficiently intelligent concept could get away with using various tools to simulate their atavisims.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T21:06:41-08:00","id":1050875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1032892-horrors-with-many-atavisms?p=1050190#post1050190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thinking on it a horror based off a sufficiently intelligent concept could get away with using various tools to simulate their atavisims.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you mean a <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/SufficientlyAdvancedAlien\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Sufficiently Advanced Alien</b></a>? If so, I agree.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}